This tree is Neroued/ninfer (https://github.com/Neroued/ninfer) with an Ada Lovelace
(sm_89, GeForce RTX 4090) port layer. The port layer derives from work published under the
same license by:

- UDPSendToFailed (https://github.com/UDPSendToFailed/ninfer-4090): the original RTX 4090
  fork; E8 Conway-Sloane lattice KV cache quantization (rk4v4-e8), rotated int4/int8 KV
  storages, the WDDM evictable-budget residency lock, DirectStorage prompt cache, Ada
  small-T MMA routes, SM-count-sized launch policies, n-gram prompt-lookup drafting,
  structured JSON output, embedded WebUI, Prometheus metrics.
- sergiuszm (https://github.com/sergiuszm/ninfer-4090): sm_89 kernel adaptation of the
  int8 attention family, rk4v4-e8 integration, GDN cooperative-launch and pairwise
  reduction fixes.
- Ambolio (https://github.com/Ambolio/ninfer-4090-windows): the sm_89 layer on upstream
  v1.0.7 that this tree replays onto v3 master: 48 KiB shared-memory schedules, Blackwell-only
  kernel exclusions and stubs, Windows MSVC build, OVERLAPPED artifact I/O.
- natpate (https://github.com/natpate/ninfer-windows) and headpiece747
  (https://github.com/headpiece747/ninfer-5090-windows): Win32/MSVC portability.
- Don-Chad (https://github.com/Don-Chad/ninfer-3090): the Ampere (sm_86) port and
  compatibility bridges the 4090 lineage grew from.
- nmorgowicz (https://github.com/nmorgowicz/ninfer-windows): --tolerant-tool-calls.
- dylanbrodiefafard (https://github.com/dylanbrodiefafard/ninfer): incremental host encode.

Model weights are Qwen (Alibaba Cloud); DFlash companion weights are from z-lab.
